<!-- FAQ.

     Native <details>, not a JS accordion: open/close then costs no script and
     is keyboard- and screen-reader-correct for free.

     Note it is NOT currently indexable. App.razor renders with
     InteractiveAutoRenderMode(prerender: false), so the whole app — this page
     included — ships an empty body and builds itself in the browser. A crawler
     that does not execute JavaScript sees none of this. Turning prerendering on
     would fix it, but it is an app-wide change and this page navigates away
     during OnInitializedAsync for signed-in users, which prerendering does not
     take kindly to. -->
<div id="faq" class="sec sec-alt"><div class="wrap" style="max-width:760px">
<div style="text-align:center">
<span class="seyebrow">Questions</span>
<h2 class="stt">Before you sign up</h2>
</div>
<div class="faqlist">

<details class="faq">
<summary>What happens to my invoices if I stop paying?</summary>
<div class="faqa"><p>Nothing is deleted. Your account moves to the Free plan and every invoice, estimate, client and time entry stays exactly where it is. Links you have already sent keep working, so a client can still open and pay an invoice you issued while on Pro. What changes is what you can create next.</p></div>
</details>

<details class="faq">
<summary>Can I get my data out?</summary>
<div class="faqa"><p>Yes, whenever you like, without asking us. Account → Personal data → Download gives you a copy. The same screen deletes your account and data outright if you would rather leave entirely.</p></div>
</details>

<details class="faq">
<summary>What counts towards the free plan's @FreeInvoiceLimit invoices a month?</summary>
<div class="faqa"><p>Invoices you create in a calendar month. The counter resets on the 1st. Clients, projects, jobs, timesheets and expenses are unlimited on every plan — the limit is only on invoices.</p></div>
</details>

<details class="faq">
<summary>How good is the translation, really?</summary>
<div class="faqa">
<p>It is two different things, and the difference matters.</p>
<p>The fixed furniture of an invoice — Subtotal, Amount Due, Bill To, Payment Options — is written into Akinai for each language, so it is always the term a local accountant expects, it renders instantly, and it costs nothing.</p>
<p>The text <em>you</em> wrote — job descriptions, notes, terms — is machine-translated. That is good enough for a client to understand what they are being billed for, and we would not tell you it is good enough for a contract. If a line carries an obligation, read it before you send it.</p>
</div>
</details>

<details class="faq">
<summary>Do I need a Vietnamese bank account?</summary>
<div class="faqa"><p>Only for VietQR, which needs Vietnamese bank details to generate the code. Everything else works from anywhere — bank transfer with IBAN and SWIFT, PayPal, Wise and Revolut — and you set payment details separately per currency, so a VND client can see VietQR while a EUR client sees your euro account.</p></div>
</details>

<details class="faq">
<summary>Does my client need an account?</summary>
<div class="faqa"><p>No, and they never will. They open a link and see the invoice in their language, or accept an estimate, or use the client portal. No signup, no password, nothing to install.</p></div>
</details>

<details class="faq">
<summary>Can I bill in a currency I don't hold?</summary>
<div class="faqa"><p>Yes, on Pro. Invoice in your client's currency with live exchange rates, and give them the account details for whichever currency you actually want to be paid in. The Free plan is single-currency.</p></div>
</details>

<details class="faq">
<summary>How does the subscription work?</summary>
<div class="faqa"><p>Card payment through Stripe, renewing monthly or annually until you stop it. Cancelling keeps you on Pro until the end of the period you have already paid for, then moves you to Free — no partial refund, and nothing removed. Full detail is in the <a href="terms">terms</a>.</p></div>
</details>

</div>
</div></div>

